Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0130: give Maps the Metal env group

Maps is a Metal-only client: VectorKit's map renderer needs an MTLDevice.
Today the app is in no sweetenv group, so it never loads bgmtl, never calls
MTLAddDevice and draws no map. The installed command line is 601 of 607
bytes, so a Maps entry of its own does not fit.

Add "Maps" to the existing @wallpaper process group (j0121). It then gets
DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES=/usr/local/p/i.dylib and BGMTL_ENABLE=1 from the
already-present @wallpaper entry, costing no boot-arg bytes. The injector
allowlist is extended separately (mesa/metal/inject/bgmtl_sweet_inject.m).

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5615,7 +5615,8 @@
 		static const char *const names[] = {
 			"AegirPoster", "CollectionsPoster", "GradientPosterExtension",
 			"PridePosterExtension", "LegacyPoster", "PhotosPosterProvider",
-			"UnityPosterExtension", "EmojiPosterExtension", "ExtragalacticPoster"
+			"UnityPosterExtension", "EmojiPosterExtension", "ExtragalacticPoster",
+			"Maps"
 		};
 		for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(names) / sizeof(names[0]); i++) {
 			if (strcmp(base, names[i]) == 0) return 1;
